message.content:
Hitch-mounted bicycle racks are generally classified as parts and accessories of motor vehicles in heading 8708, specifically 8708.99 "Other parts and accessories." CBP rulings on hitch-mounted bike racks have gone to 8708.99.8180 (other parts and accessories, other). Other rulings have classified roof racks in 8708.99.8180 as well. Since the racks are made of aluminum and steel, an alternative would be 8714.10 (parts of motorcycles) or 8714.91, but 8714 covers bicycle parts, and a rack that mounts on a vehicle is not a part of a bicycle. Heading 8708 is therefore the best fit.

The current statistical suffix for 8708.99.81 is 8708.99.8180 ("Other"), after the 2022 revisions. The 8708.99.68 subheading is for other parts and accessories, and 8708.99.81 is for other, so I'll use 8708.99.8180.

{"hts_code": "8708.99.8180", "reason": "Hitch-mounted bicycle racks are designed for use with motor vehicles and are classified as other parts and accessories of motor vehicles under heading 8708, in the residual subheading 8708.99.81."}
